  "checks": [
    "GUA1: monic characteristic-polynomial factorization detects Tor on each block; N=0 and unramified twists retain precisely the source predicate.",
    "GUA2: original PlainTor permits repeated rank-one constituents but excludes linked singleton segments; the original universal IsRecT rank-one and twist laws prove full PlainGd.",
    "GUA3: directly read LanglandsMultisegments: its second clause is exactly the constituent-of-product assertion used here. No intermediate product irreducibility is assumed.",
    "GUA4–6: shared BCS8 is the only published generic-unitary application; central-character precedence x+1<=y and strict half bounds give ordered Speh cosocles. The combined exponent is (d_i-2k-n)/2 after the one algNorm twist.",
    "GUA7: directly checked PropsB/AwayB/AboveB and Row0b. Tor is a separate nice disjunct, so no large-prime or Qp/rank constraint is imported. Every original A,h,rc,O,LocBridge,Induces and induced embedding is retained.",
    "GUA8: actual |det|^s cusp twist has s=(e+a-1)/2; norm pullback of the polarizing Hecke character is xi^2 and its real sign is (-1)^a. Rec algNorm and HT identities give e/2 and -z-e/2 exactly without a half cyclotomic Galois character.",
    "GUA9–11: the original dominant weight multiset is simple, giving every shifted constituent regular/integral. Finite period sums use common finite coefficients and each given bridge. One actual block representation is chosen; irreducibility forces exactly one positive block and length one.",
    "GUA12: compact induction H-module argument establishes spherical irreducible uniqueness; K-fixed induction is exact. The determinant character and multisegment uniqueness force spherical segments to have length one. The resulting unramified rank-one parameters satisfy every IsRecT, with reciprocal arithmetic Satake roots.",
    "GUA13–14: source HasSat agrees on actual isotypic local components; BCS19 supplies every IsUnramU place. Direct FrobTotT/FrobEig/algSat check gives geometric roots q_w^((n-1)/2) beta. Expanded IsWDOf proof kills original full inertia from N=0, finite inertia image and the semisimple/nilpotent comparison; every valuation and Frobenius lift is retained.",
    "GUA15–17: all split local components give the same parameter; PlainTor supplies universal goodness. Conjugation and inverse Satake roots yield R^c=R^vee epsilon^(1-n) for every prescribed conjugation via cofinite Chebotarev. Positive-block irreducibility gives the actual rank-n cusp with all original AttC, infinity, spherical and split-component fields.",
    "GUA18: all literal GalUnitaryT fields and the GuWrap endpoint compared directly; original RowT, local correspondence existence, period foundations and named base change remain stated inputs."
  ],
